# Testing Dude locally (agents)

When verifying Dude behavior, use this workflow instead of guessing URLs or APIs.

## 1. Start dev

```sh
npm run dev
```

Confirm: `npm run agent:status` (exit 0). Client `http://127.0.0.1:5173`, API `http://127.0.0.1:8787`.

If API is down, chat turns fail with gateway/proxy 500 — fix API first, not the UI.

## 2. Choose test mode

| Mode | When |
|------|------|
| **API** (`npm run agent -- chat …`) | Logic, tools, agent completion without UI |
| **Browser MCP** | Layout, TipTap/canvas, streaming UI, clicks |
| **Both** | Create workspace via CLI, open `openUrl` in browser, send prompt in UI |

## 3. CLI harness

```sh
npm run agent -- workspaces create --specialist document-writer --name "Agent test"
npm run agent -- chat --specialist document-writer --workspace <id> --message "..."
npm run agent -- browser-hints --specialist document-writer --workspace <id>
```

Full reference: `scripts/agent-harness/README.md`.

## 4. Browser MCP (`cursor-ide-browser`)

1. `browser_navigate` → URL from `npm run agent -- url --specialist <id> [--workspace <id>]`
2. `browser_lock` → interact → `browser_unlock`
3. After agent work, CDP evaluate:

```javascript
window.__DUDE_AGENT__?.snapshot()
```

Document Writer canvas: `window.__DUDE_DW_DEBUG__?.snapshot()` — expect `blockCount > 0` after edits.

## 5. Specialist IDs

`main-assistant`, `data-analyst`, `document-writer`, `presentation-editor`, `design-branding`, `prospect`

## 6. Do not

- Commit or log `.env.local` secrets
- Assume `/health` on API root — use `agent:status` (checks `/healthz`, `/v1/health`, `/api/health`)
- Skip `npm run dev` when testing integrated chat/gateway flows
